    "body": "## Motivation\n\nA NGRAM cache flush can be undone by already queued inserts. The final verification step submits corpus updates asynchronously; `clear_cache_pool()` calls `reset()` without first synchronizing those updates. The reset clears the online trie, but the insertion worker can then repopulate it with pre-flush sequences.\n\nAn unchanged native corpus returned the old continuation after enqueue → reset → synchronize in 25/25 runs. The actual Python → TVM FFI path reproduced the same behavior in 10/10 runs.\n\n## Modifications\n\nWait for the existing pending-insert counter to reach zero before resetting the trie and match state. The condition-variable wait releases the existing mutex so the insertion worker can finish; reset retains the mutex from observing zero through clearing. External corpora remain loaded, and inserts admitted after reset can populate the fresh online cache.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Two new regression methods cover pending inserts with BFS/PROB matching, subsequent new inserts, and preservation of an external corpus. The original source fails three assertions; the corrected source passes.\n- Complete existing NGRAM corpus suite: 40 test methods passed and one class-level skip; the existing HTTP mock test class is skipped because importing http_server requires unavailable CUDA libraries.\n- Matching pre-commit hooks and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nLocal tests compile all five actual native/FFI source files and execute the original Python wrappers on CPU. The harness substitutes CPU build discovery for GPU-target discovery and excludes test-only GPU-idle/retry services. No GPU generation or model-output accuracy run is claimed. The backlog reproduction is repeated observed evidence, not a forced thread schedule.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo inference-speed claim. The change only waits during reset; steady-state insertion and matching paths are unchanged. A flush may now wait for already admitted insertions before clearing them.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with matching pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] Add unit tests to the existing CPU-registered NGRAM suite.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n- [ ] Documentation update: no API or configuration change.\n- [ ] GPU accuracy/speed benchmarks: not run; validation is the CPU corpus lifecycle above.\n\nAI assistance was used for implementation, tests, and review.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36896397172](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36896397172)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36896396563](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36896396563)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36896396803](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36896396803)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
